Z||000006||DJRice||07-18-2000||02:35 PM||||Two weeks ago my brother was apartment hunting and happend to notice a Fiero just like his in one of the apartments he checked out.  He didnt think much of it, but a week later went back to that Apartment Complex because he decided he liked what they had to offer.  This time, my dad happened to be with him and they passed the Fiero, which was now wrecked.  <P>Upon closer inspection of the car, he found a note that said "Please dont tow, we dont have the money to get it out of impound and we have a loan against the title."<P>My dad offered the guy $250 and he accepted.  He even was able to produce a clean title a couple of days later.  <P>The car is also an 85GT with 131K and all options but the subwoofer.  The guys daugther stole the car and bounced it off a tree (Right front side is mangled, probably bent frame).  I hate to see a car torn up like that, but hey, it worked out good for us!<P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
